<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB WINS $244 MLN CZECH ORDER.</title>
<headline>ABB WINS $244 MLN CZECH ORDER.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electrical engineering group ABB Asea Brown Boveri AG said it had received an order valued at 244 million to build a 330-megawatt coal and gas-fired combined heat and power plant at Kladno, outside Prague.</p>
<p>The order was placed by the independent power producer Energeticke Centrum Kladno Generating (ECK Generating) and is one of the largest ever placed in Central and Eastern Europe for an independent power project, ABB said in a statement.</p>
</text>
